JSON data obtained through an API call can be nested at multiple levels, making it difficult to analyze. Fortunately, Polars can read JSON data at multiple levels, ensuring that the data is fully un-nested. Below is some JSON data to load into a dataframe.

::: {#b1932641 .cell execution_count=1}
``` {.python .cell-code}
data = [
    {
        "id": 1,
        "name": "Dan Humphrey",
        "fitness": {"height": 180, "weight": 85},
    },
    {
        "id": 2,
        "name": "Blair Waldolf",
        "fitness": {"height": 155, "weight": 58},
    }
]
```
:::


## Read data at level zero

We can start by unnesting the first level. This will return a three-column dataframe:

::: {#2f816c02 .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import polars as pl

pl.json_normalize(data, max_level=0)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (2, 3)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>id</th><th>name</th><th>fitness</th></tr><tr><td>i64</td><td>str</td><td>str</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>&quot;Dan Humphrey&quot;</td><td>&quot;{&quot;height&quot;: 180, &quot;weight&quot;: 85}&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>&quot;Blair Waldolf&quot;</td><td>&quot;{&quot;height&quot;: 155, &quot;weight&quot;: 58}&quot;</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


## Read data at level one

Some nested data remains in the *fitness* column. We can unnest it by increasing the level by 1:

::: {#6b391293 .cell execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
pl.json_normalize(data, max_level=1)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}
```{=html}
<div><style>
.dataframe > thead > tr,
.dataframe > tbody > tr {
  text-align: right;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
}
</style>
<small>shape: (2, 4)</small><table border="1" class="dataframe"><thead><tr><th>id</th><th>name</th><th>fitness.height</th><th>fitness.weight</th></tr><tr><td>i64</td><td>str</td><td>i64</td><td>i64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>&quot;Dan Humphrey&quot;</td><td>180</td><td>85</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>&quot;Blair Waldolf&quot;</td><td>155</td><td>58</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
```
:::
:::


